# Htrow-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Htrowelzzif (Sorcerer who fights with a
# longsword and shield). Drop it into a bigshot hunting-commands list as a
# single command:
#
#   script Htrow-attack
#
# Built on Brayis-attack.lic rather than Fizzleworth's sorcerer scripts: she has
# no Magic Item Use, so there's no wand fallback -- the finisher is her sword.
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has
# locked, then resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does ONE pass of
# her rotation per call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while the
# target is still up. Death is read off GameObj status (what bigshot itself
# uses), not a per-creature kill-message regex.
#
# Each pass (Scott's rotation, 10/30):
#
#   stance guarded, then each spell in opener_spells -- Blood Burst (701), then
#     Mana Disruption (702) -- each only if live mana covers it;
#   stance offensive, then a plain attack with the longsword.
#
# and bigshot's next call repeats it until the target is dead.
#
# Why a script for it: bigshot's hunting_stance (Offensive) re-sends "stance
# offensive" before every command, so in a bigshot command list the guard never
# lasted to the casts (10/30 log: "stanc guard", "[bigshot]>stance offensive",
# "incant 701"). In here nothing comes between the guard and the casts.
#
# NOTE on Tenebrous Tether (706), which her list used to cast second: it's a
# concentration spell and her next swing breaks it. On 10/30 all 10 targets it
# rooted were freed by the very next attack ("...your concentration on the
# spell is broken."), so each one bought about two seconds of root for 6 mana.
# Replaced by Disintegrate (705), then by 702, which costs 2 mana to 705's 5.
#
# OVEREXERTION: a cast without its full mana in hand still goes through and
# hurts you, so each one is gated on the live checkmana against its cost,
# re-read right before the incant (after the previous cast drained mana) --
# the job (m1)/(m2) would do in a bigshot list. Short on mana just means fewer
# casts; the sword swing happens either way.
#
# FREE ACCOUNT: she can't hunt carrying 5,000+ silver -- every cast and swing
# just gets "[Because your account is free, you cannot hunt while carrying 5000
# silvers or more. ...]" (21 times on 10/30, after eherbs withdrew 8,000 for
# herbs and kept the change). A refused swing has no roundtime, so without a
# check bigshot would re-run this script in a tight loop. A persistent hook
# notes that message; the pass that sees it asks bigshot to rest instead
# (reason "Carrying 5,000+ silver"), and Htrow-prerest.lic banks the coins.
#
# DISARM (from Brayis-attack.lic, where a death dirge disarmed Brayis twice and
# he died fighting bare-fisted): her shield stays in the LEFT hand after a
# disarm, so the check is the sword hand (right) being empty, not both hands.
# On an empty right hand it tries GIRD once (the sword may just be in the
# cloak); if that still leaves it empty it prints a DISARMED banner, sets
# $bigshot_should_rest (reason "Disarmed") and exits without attacking.
# Htrow-prep.lic stops bigshot in town if GIRD comes up empty there too.
# A persistent DownstreamHook records the room any "Use the RECOVER ITEM
# command" line arrives in, since a disarm can land while bigshot is walking.

# --- knobs (methods, so an edit applies on the next pass without a relog) ----

# Spells cast at the target every pass, in this order, before the swing.
def opener_spells
  [701, 702]
end

# Mana for one cast. Spell#mana_cost reads Lich's effect-list.xml (701 = 1,
# 702 = 2); the table is only the fallback if that lookup comes back empty.
def spell_mana(num)
  cost = (Spell[num].mana_cost.to_i rescue 0)
  cost.positive? ? cost : { 701 => 1, 702 => 2, 705 => 5, 706 => 6 }.fetch(num, 99)
end

# --- patterns ----------------------------------------------------------------

# A wound bad enough to block casting -- no roundtime, and every other cast
# would fail the same way, so the pass skips straight to the sword.
CANT_CAST_WOUNDED = /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i unless defined?(CANT_CAST_WOUNDED)

# Still in cast roundtime from the last spell: the incant didn't go out.
CAST_WAIT = /^\s*\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i unless defined?(CAST_WAIT)

# The end of one cast's output (or one of the two refusals above).
CAST_DONE = /Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Roundtime: \d+ sec|can't think clearly enough to prepare|^\s*\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i unless defined?(CAST_DONE)

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages
# (they vary per creature) -- it reads GameObj status, which Lich core keeps
# current from the room/combat XML. A dead creature reads "dead" while the
# corpse lingers, then "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Sends one incant and returns everything it printed, up to its cast roundtime
# line (or the wound block / a "Wait N sec." refusal, neither of which gets
# one). clear first so lines left over from the previous cast -- its blood
# burst ticks, its own roundtime line -- can't end this read early.
def cast_collect(cmd, timeout = 6)
  lines = []
  clear
  put cmd
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + timeout
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      lines << line
      break if line =~ CAST_DONE
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= deadline
  end
  lines.join("\n")
end

def go_guarded
  fput "stance guarded" if stance != "guarded"
end

def can_afford?(num)
  checkmana >= spell_mana(num)
end

# Each opener spell in turn, from guarded. A spell she can't afford is skipped,
# not the whole list -- a cheaper one after it may still fit. Stops early if
# the target dies or a wound blocks casting.
def cast_openers(foe)
  opener_spells.each do |num|
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    next unless can_afford?(num)
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    next unless can_afford?(num)   # re-read right before the incant
    go_guarded
    text = cast_collect("incant #{num}")
    if text =~ CAST_WAIT
      # Sleep the seconds the game gave: right after a swing, Lich may not have
      # registered its roundtime yet, so waitrt? alone returns at once and the
      # retry gets refused too (10/30 11:54:51, "...wait 4 seconds." -- that
      # pass lost its 701).
      secs = text[/wait (\d+) sec/i, 1].to_i
      sleep([secs, 5].min) if secs.positive?
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      return if target_dead?(foe)
      next unless can_afford?(num)
      text = cast_collect("incant #{num}")
    end
    return if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
  end
end

# Offensive, then one swing with the longsword. No-ops if the openers already
# killed it.
def finish_attack(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"
  fput "attack"
  waitrt?
end

# --- disarm handling ---------------------------------------------------------

# GS4 prints this for EVERY way of having an item knocked away (a death dirge's
# voice, a hardened-hide rebound, a curse, ...), so one pattern covers them all.
HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_MSG = /Use the RECOVER ITEM command/i unless defined?(HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_MSG)

# How long a recorded disarm room is still believed when reporting it.
HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_FRESH_SECS = 1800 unless defined?(HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_FRESH_SECS)

# Remembers WHERE the disarm line arrived. bigshot re-invokes this script every
# pass and a disarm can land while bigshot is walking between passes, so the
# recording has to live in a hook that outlives each pass: persist: true is
# what stops Lich removing it when this script exits. Re-adding it each pass
# just replaces it under the same name.
# To remove it: ;e DownstreamHook.remove('htrowelzzif_disarm_room')
DownstreamHook.add('htrowelzzif_disarm_room', proc { |server_string|
  begin
    if server_string =~ HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_MSG
      room = Room.current
      $htrowelzzif_disarm = { room: room&.id, title: Array(room&.title).first, at: Time.now }
    end
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end
  server_string
}, persist: true)

# GIRD puts the longsword in the right hand and the shield in the left, and a
# disarm only takes the sword -- so the right hand is the one that matters.
def sword_hand_empty?
  checkright.nil?
end

# Report the disarm loudly and send bigshot to rest rather than fight on with
# just a shield. Htrow-prep.lic then stops bigshot if GIRD finds no sword.
def handle_disarmed
  info  = $htrowelzzif_disarm
  fresh = info && (Time.now - info[:at]) < HTROWELZZIF_DISARM_FRESH_SECS
  here  = Room.current
  echo "########## DISARMED -- no sword in the right hand ##########"
  if fresh
    echo "## the RECOVER ITEM line arrived #{(Time.now - info[:at]).round}s ago in room #{info[:room]} (#{info[:title]})"
  else
    echo "## disarm room unknown (no recent RECOVER ITEM line seen); noticed in room #{here&.id} (#{Array(here&.title).first})"
  end
  echo "## not fighting with just a shield -- asking bigshot to rest"
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Disarmed"
end

# --- free-account silver cap ---------------------------------------------------

HTROW_SILVER_CAP_MSG = /account is free, you cannot hunt while carrying/i unless defined?(HTROW_SILVER_CAP_MSG)

# Notes when the game refuses a cast or swing over the silver cap. A hook rather
# than reading each command's reply so it also catches the refusal of a command
# bigshot sent itself between passes.
# To remove it: ;e DownstreamHook.remove('htrow_silver_cap')
DownstreamHook.add('htrow_silver_cap', proc { |server_string|
  begin
    $htrow_silver_capped_at = Time.now if server_string =~ HTROW_SILVER_CAP_MSG
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end
  server_string
}, persist: true)

def silver_capped?
  $htrow_silver_capped_at && (Time.now - $htrow_silver_capped_at) < 20
end

def rest_for_silver_cap
  echo "########## carrying 5,000+ silver -- a free account can't hunt with that ##########"
  echo "## asking bigshot to rest; Htrow-prerest banks it"
  $htrow_silver_capped_at = nil
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Carrying 5,000+ silver"
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?
waitcastrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if silver_capped?
  rest_for_silver_cap
  exit
end

# Empty sword hand: try GIRD once (the sword may only be in the cloak), and
# only call it a disarm if that doesn't bring it back.
if sword_hand_empty?
  fput "gird"
  pause 0.5
  if sword_hand_empty?
    handle_disarmed
    exit
  end
end

# A crash in the openers should cost one pass's spells, not the swing --
# otherwise bigshot re-runs a crashing script in a tight loop (Felix, 10/27).
begin
  cast_openers(foe)
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "Htrow-attack: openers failed (#{e.class}: #{e.message}) -- swinging anyway"
end

finish_attack(foe)

rest_for_silver_cap if silver_capped?
